            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "dianamtu"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This will be the 3rd time making this pie and i lovee that it's so easy. I used 1/2 c sugar, 2 T cornstarch, and about 2.5 T sugar free strawberry jello. Cut the berries only in half, mixed with the glaze, and let it set overnight. Turned out perfect with just the right mix of tart and sweet."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "DFBROWN"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Good but a little too sweet and to much gelatin but well worth modifying. Next time I will try reducing gelatine to 3 packages and reduce sugar to 1/3 cup sugar.",
            "datePublished": "2002-04-09T18:36:00.733Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "janwan15"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yes, I will make pie again. My pie was very good and not too sweet but just right. I made my own glaze and also did the layer of cream cheese with confectioners sugar as one member suggested.",
            "datePublished": "2019-10-08T00:32:39.413Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sarge"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I put 8 oz of cream cheese on the crust to give it a savory or more bold taste. It was very delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2017-07-04T19:43:12.220Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I didn't have Jell-O, so I substituted 2 packets of Knox gelatin + 2 T sugar (in addition to the 2/3c) plus 1 tsp strawberry extract. And I made it in a gluten-free pie crust. Turned out great!!",
            "datePublished": "2024-06-19T12:44:22.580Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Psm"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made it. Everyone liked it. I would use less sugar next time, maybe only 1/4 c. I'd like to try the sugar free jello but if I do I'll start with only 1T. It seems that the sugar free is really sweet. I made it the day before so it chilled about 15 hours before serving and we all were amazed at how perfectly the pieces came out.",
            "datePublished": "2016-06-20T19:37:26.773Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "PMommy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Divine! Added the layer of cream cheese (8oz) &amp; powdered sugar (2T) as suggested. Used only 1/4c. sugar in the glaze because strawberries were very sweet. Used graham cracker crust I recipe from this site. Had to make it two nights in a row because the demand was so great from my family. Can't wait to try it with peaches.",
            "datePublished": "2010-04-08T15:42:20.547Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ashleynicole"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Cut recipe in 1/2. Used exact ingredients ratios and directions. Used shortbread crust (1c flour, 1/2c butter, 1/4c powdered sugar, 1t vanilla) instead of graham crust and i'm really glad i did. After pouring strawberry filling into crust I stuck it in the freezer instead of the fridge for a while to set up cuz i get impatient. Served the pie with cool whip. Flavor of this pie is amazing. not too sweet just perfect.",
            "datePublished": "2009-03-15T12:59:21.230Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Rich562"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Extremely good glaze. On my second attempt, I added 1/2 tsp \"Vitamin C Granules\" to the recipe, since I love a tart fruit pies. That did the trick. If you like a sweet glaze, this one is great. If you like a little tart kick, try adding the Vitamin C. Also, be sure you let the glaze cool to at least 80 degrees before adding to the strawberries.",
            "datePublished": "2011-06-25T13:45:44.177Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "franuhle"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Best strawberry glaze ever. I put a cream cheese layer - whipped and sweetened with a bit of sugar on the crust, then chilled it. Then put on whole berries which I tossed in glaze first, then the balance of glaze over all.\nNo restaurant pie can touch it. Gorgeous and delicious.",
            "datePublished": "2011-04-24T12:00:33.567Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jill Davis Forshey"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made it night before. When I served the following evening it wasn't as glossy. I made two. I did make one with sugar and cream cheese on top of layer of graham crust. Someone recommend that to avoid soggy crust. The one without cream cheese was not soggy. The cream cheese mixture was hard to spread, maybe it didn't have enough sugar. To do over I'd make the morning of or 4 hours before serving. Made my own crust with graham's. Definitely will try with peaches.",
            "datePublished": "2017-01-31T21:12:48.160Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "JosephA"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I was eager to make a sweet dessert with fresh strawberries. Nothing says summer louder than strawberries! Ok, will maybe watermelon does. Anyway, I followed the recipe save two revisions. I used a 0.44 oz. box of sugar free gelatin mix instead of the prescribed 4 Tbsp. and added only 2 Tbsp. of cornstarch instead of twice that. I agreed with others who that that excessive. While the pie glaze had a somewhat \"jello\" flavor, the fresh strawberries overshadowed this almost enough. It was not overly sweet as I expect it would be with the store bought glaze.",
            "datePublished": "2026-07-12T03:55:46.681Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kathy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My family has made this pie for years. We call it Big Boy Pie. My husband was a diabetic so I substituted sugar free strawberry Jello and used substituted Equal for the sugar, it made absolutely no difference in fast or texture. 🍓😍😍",
            "datePublished": "2026-07-11T22:35:07.673Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Amber123"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This turned out really great. Absolutely would make it again. It’s not a lot of work to make the glaze and I feel better about using that than the neon red glaze from the grocery store. I would probably add a tsp or two of vanilla to the glaze to bump up the flavor. I’ll also try adding the cream cheese layer next time too.",
            "datePublished": "2026-04-23T17:06:15.872Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lois"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this following the recipe exactly and it was so good! My husband loved it too, and I will make this in the future. I like that the strawberries are sliced so the glaze is equally distributed throughout the berries. Very easy to make!",
            "datePublished": "2026-04-20T05:58:05.640Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
